<title>USA: Cole National Q1 May 3 net rises.</title>
<headline>Cole National Q1 May 3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997	   1996</p>
<p> Net revenue				    249,530	 142,890</p>
<p> Income from operations			12,602	   6,803</p>
<p> Net income					 2,448	     980</p>
<p> Earnings per share				0.20	    0.09</p>
<p> Weighted average shares		 12,019,488    10,435,423</p>
<p>(Results in 000s except per share)</p>
<p>NOTES: The company said rise in revenues and profits was driven by acquisition of Pearle Vision in November 1996, a 10.9 percent increase in Cole Vision's same-store sales and growth in managed vision care sale.</p>
<p>Same-store sales for Pearle unit's rose 2.6 percent. Same-store sales for Cole's Things Remembered and Cole Gift Center fell 3.1 percent and 6.1 percent, respectively, because of a drop in mall traffic, Cole said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
